    "content": "<h3>Anura</h3>\n<p>Anura have the traits of frogs and toads, though their animalistic traits can be hard to spot, mostly shown in their eyes, and in patches of scales over their bodies. Anura internally produce a very potent toxin which they can secrete through glands on their neck and back. As such, they are often skilled in toxicology and use of these poisons and toxins; it is a reputation that precedes them, as many are fearful of the Anura, fearing to even touch them, or eat food that they’ve prepared. However, the Anura are capable of controlling the toxicity of their poison, and thus pose little actual risk.<br>The Anura are rare, originating from the rainforests of Sargon and Bolivar. These humid, swampy regions suit their natural constitution, and thus they sometimes come into contact with the Archosaurians who also dwell in these regions. In modern times, some Anura are beginning to migrate from their rainforest home into nomadic cities; though they still prefer those with abundant greenery and good access to water.</p>\n<h4>Anuran Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Creature Type:</em></strong> You are a Humanoid.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Size:</em></strong> Anura stand between 5 and 5.5 feet, and average 130 pounds. Your size is Medium.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Life Expectancy:</em></strong> Anura reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Speed:</em></strong> Your base Walking Speed is 30 feet. You have a Swimming Speed equal to your Walking Speed.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Intelligence Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.</p>\n<h4>Anuran Features</h4>\n<p>As an Anura, you gain the following features:</p>\n<h5>Blood of the Swamp</h5>\n<p>The Anura are naturally toxic, and originate from deep, dank swamps full of equally venomous creatures. They have developed a strong resistance to all toxins. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p><strong>Legacy of Venom.</strong> You have Advantage on Saving Throws you make to avoid or end the Poisoned Condition or the effect of any Toxin.</p>\n<p><strong>Poison Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Poison Damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-Toxin Immunity.</strong> You are immune to the Damage and Effects of Toxins you produce using your Toxin Glands Feature.</p>\n<h5>Toxin Glands</h5>\n<p>The Anura can secrete their venom to make use of it in their lives; as such, they have a somewhat unsavoury reputation in the wider world outside of their tribes. Many are afraid to touch them, to share utensils, or to even eat food prepared by them.<br>Once per Short Rest, you can secrete 1x Cytotoxin as an Action. If this toxin is not used within 10 minutes, it becomes inert.<br>From 7th Level, you can secrete 1x Neurotoxin instead.</p>\n<h5>Partially Amphibious</h5>\n<p>The Anura are not a purely water-dwelling people, but they have dwelled in and around water for as long as any in their homelands can recall.<br>You can hold your breath for twice as long as normal.</p>\n<h5>Ancient Versatility</h5>\n<p>The Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:</p>\n<p><strong>Durable.</strong> Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.</p>\n<p><strong>Reliable.</strong> You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.</p>\n<p><strong>Tenacious.</strong> You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Anura\nAnura have the traits of frogs and toads, though their animalistic traits can be hard to spot, mostly shown in their eyes, and in patches of scales over their bodies. Anura internally produce a very potent toxin which they can secrete through glands on their neck and back. As such, they are often skilled in toxicology and use of these poisons and toxins; it is a reputation that precedes them, as many are fearful of the Anura, fearing to even touch them, or eat food that they’ve prepared. However, the Anura are capable of controlling the toxicity of their poison, and thus pose little actual risk.\n:\nThe Anura are rare, originating from the rainforests of Sargon and Bolivar. These humid, swampy regions suit their natural constitution, and thus they sometimes come into contact with the Archosaurians who also dwell in these regions. In modern times, some Anura are beginning to migrate from their rainforest home into nomadic cities; though they still prefer those with abundant greenery and good access to water. \n\n#### Anuran Traits\n\n***Creature Type:*** You are a Humanoid. \n\n***Size:*** Anura stand between 5 and 5.5 feet, and average 130 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\n***Life Expectancy:*** Anura reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years.\n\n***Speed:*** Your base Walking Speed is 30 feet. You have a Swimming Speed equal to your Walking Speed.\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Intelligence Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.\n\n#### Anuran Features\nAs an Anura, you gain the following features:\n\n##### Blood of the Swamp\nThe Anura are naturally toxic, and originate from deep, dank swamps full of equally venomous creatures. They have developed a strong resistance to all toxins. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Legacy of Venom.** You have Advantage on Saving Throws you make to avoid or end the Poisoned Condition or the effect of any Toxin. \n\n**Poison Resistance.** You have Resistance to Poison Damage. \n\n**Self-Toxin Immunity.** You are immune to the Damage and Effects of Toxins you produce using your Toxin Glands Feature.\n\n\\column\n\n##### Toxin Glands\nThe Anura can secrete their venom to make use of it in their lives; as such, they have a somewhat unsavoury reputation in the wider world outside of their tribes. Many are afraid to touch them, to share utensils, or to even eat food prepared by them. \n:\nOnce per Short Rest, you can secrete 1x Cytotoxin as an Action. If this toxin is not used within 10 minutes, it becomes inert. \n:\nFrom 7th Level, you can secrete 1x Neurotoxin instead. \n\n##### Partially Amphibious\nThe Anura are not a purely water-dwelling people, but they have dwelled in and around water for as long as any in their homelands can recall.\n:\nYou can hold your breath for twice as long as normal.\n\n##### Ancient Versatility\nThe Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:\n\n**Durable.** Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.\n\n**Reliable.** You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.\n\n**Tenacious.** You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.\n\n\n<img \nsrc='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/7/7f/Blue_Poison_Elite_2.png' style='position:absolute;top:660px;right:-140px;width:650px;clip-path:rect(auto 80% 48% auto);' />\n\n\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}\n\\page\n\n\n{{wide"
