    "content": "<h3>Feline</h3>\n<p>Felines are humanoids with Feliform traits, shown prominently in ears, tails, eye colour, and teeth structure. Much like their namesake, they have a reputation for stealth (if not outright guile). They are the most populous race on Terra, able to adapt to any and all circumstances. Such is their ubiquity that a Gaulish proverb \"Où que tu ailles, un Félin suit (Wherever you go, a Feline follows)\" has outlived the empire that it originated from.<br>Despite being one of the most populous races on the surface of Terra, Felines have never ruled a land of their own, always serving under the banner of another. They are leal and able allies, found anywhere and everywhere, but they have never yet had a land to call home.</p>\n<h4>Feline Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Creature Type:</em></strong> You are a Humanoid.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Size:</em></strong> Felines stand between 5 and 6 feet, and average 140 pounds. Your size is Medium.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Life Expectancy:</em></strong> Felines reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Speed:</em></strong> Your base Walking Speed is 30 feet. You have a Climbing Speed equal to your Walking Speed.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Dexterity Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.</p>\n<h4>Feline Features</h4>\n<p>As a Feline, you gain the following Features:</p>\n<h5>Cat's Agility</h5>\n<p>Cats always land on their feet, or so the saying goes. Whatever the truth, Felines are undoubtedly agile. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p><strong>On Your Feet.</strong> You can rise from a Prone position at the cost of 5 feet of Movement.</p>\n<p><strong>Terminal Velocity</strong>. Whenever you would take Damage as a result of falling, you can use your Reaction to halve the damage you take from that fall.</p>\n<h5>Darkvision</h5>\n<p>The specially adapted eyes of the Felines give you a distinct advantage. You gain 120 feet of Darkvision.</p>\n<h5>Natural Skulkers</h5>\n<p>Felines are naturally adapted to quiet, stealthy movement. Even the most heavyfooted Feline can be far stealthier than they have any right to be. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p><strong>Footpad.</strong> Whenever you make a Stealth Check, if the result on the d20 is less than your Proficiency Bonus, it becomes equal to your Proficiency Bonus.</p>\n<p><strong>Stealth Proficiency.</strong> You gain Proficiency in Stealth.</p>\n<h5>Ancient Versatility</h5>\n<p>The Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:</p>\n<p><strong>Durable.</strong> Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.</p>\n<p><strong>Reliable.</strong> You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.</p>\n<p><strong>Tenacious.</strong> You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Feline\nFelines are humanoids with Feliform traits, shown prominently in ears, tails, eye colour, and teeth structure. Much like their namesake, they have a reputation for stealth (if not outright guile). They are the most populous race on Terra, able to adapt to any and all circumstances. Such is their ubiquity that a Gaulish proverb \"Où que tu ailles, un Félin suit (Wherever you go, a Feline follows)\" has outlived the empire that it originated from.\n:\nDespite being one of the most populous races on the surface of Terra, Felines have never ruled a land of their own, always serving under the banner of another. They are leal and able allies, found anywhere and everywhere, but they have never yet had a land to call home.\n\n<img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/6/68/Kal%27tsit.png' \n  style='position:absolute;top:310px;right:190px;width:750px' />\n\n\\column\n\n#### Feline Traits\n\n***Creature Type:*** You are a Humanoid.\n\n***Size:*** Felines stand between 5 and 6 feet, and average 140 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\n***Life Expectancy:*** Felines reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years. \n\n***Speed:*** Your base Walking Speed is 30 feet. You have a Climbing Speed equal to your Walking Speed.\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Dexterity Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.\n\n\n#### Feline Features\nAs a Feline, you gain the following Features:\n\n##### Cat's Agility\nCats always land on their feet, or so the saying goes. Whatever the truth, Felines are undoubtedly agile. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**On Your Feet.** You can rise from a Prone position at the cost of 5 feet of Movement.\n\n**Terminal Velocity**. Whenever you would take Damage as a result of falling, you can use your Reaction to halve the damage you take from that fall.\n\n##### Darkvision\nThe specially adapted eyes of the Felines give you a distinct advantage. You gain 120 feet of Darkvision.\n\n##### Natural Skulkers\nFelines are naturally adapted to quiet, stealthy movement. Even the most heavyfooted Feline can be far stealthier than they have any right to be. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Footpad.** Whenever you make a Stealth Check, if the result on the d20 is less than your Proficiency Bonus, it becomes equal to your Proficiency Bonus. \n\n**Stealth Proficiency.** You gain Proficiency in Stealth. \n\n##### Ancient Versatility\nThe Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:\n\n**Durable.** Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.\n\n**Reliable.** You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.\n\n**Tenacious.** You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}\n\n\\page"
