    "content": "<h3>Kuranta</h3>\n<p>Kuranta are fast and potent fighters, running down their foes in a blur of speed and moving to the next without pause. Their strength and speed come from the animals they inherit from; equines. Tall of stature, bearing funnel-shaped ears and long-haired tails, they lack the raw strength of Ursi or Forte, but none can match a Kuranta for stamina.<br>Most Kuranta originate from Kazimierz; a land torn between traditionalist feudal beliefs and modern capitalism. As such, many Kuranta subscribe to one of these ideals, of the old honour, or the new progress. Of course, some choose a different path; a middle path, or neither path.</p>\n<h4>Kuranta Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Creature Type:</em></strong> You are a Humanoid.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Size:</em></strong> Kuranta are marginally taller than some other races, clocking in between 5 and a half and 6 feet on average, but pack a lot of dense muscle into their frames; thus, they weigh about 190 pounds on average. Their size is Medium.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Life Expectancy:</em></strong> Kuranta reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Speed:</em></strong> Your base walking speed is 30 feet.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Constitution Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.</p>\n<h4>Kuranta Features</h4>\n<p>As a Kuranta, you gain the following Features:</p>\n<h5>Ever Onward</h5>\n<p>No matter their destiny, no matter their objective, no matter how hopeless; the Kuranta charge onwards.<br>When you would be subjected to an effect that would decrease your Speed or prevent you from moving, you may expend 1d8 Hit Points as a Reaction to ignore that aspect of the effect. All other aspects of the triggering effect (such as Damage dealt, and other Conditions) are applied as normal.</p>\n<h5>Run Them Down</h5>\n<p>Kuranta are naturally suited to battle by their stunning speed, opening up the opportunities for those lightning fast clashes that make the Kuranta Knights of Kazimierz so enthralling to watch.<br>You may take the Dash Action as a Bonus Action; when you do so using this Feature, you lose 1d8 Hit Points.</p>\n<h5>Until the Last Breath</h5>\n<p>Kuranta are skilled fighters; this is something everybody knows. When you see their blinding speed and bravery, it is easy to assume those are the only reasons. Under the skin, however, the hidden engine of their power pulses hot; they don’t have to beat you, just outlast you.<br>You may activate this Feature as a Bonus Action; for the next minute you gain 1d6 + your Constitution Modifier (minimum of 1) Temporary Hit Points at the beginning of each of your Turns. Once you have used this Feature, you may not do so again until you have completed a Long Rest.</p>\n<h5>Ancient Versatility</h5>\n<p>The Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:</p>\n<p><strong>Durable.</strong> Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.</p>\n<p><strong>Reliable.</strong> You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.</p>\n<p><strong>Tenacious.</strong> You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Kuranta\n\nKuranta are fast and potent fighters, running down their foes in a blur of speed and moving to the next without pause. Their strength and speed come from the animals they inherit from; equines. Tall of stature, bearing funnel-shaped ears and long-haired tails, they lack the raw strength of Ursi or Forte, but none can match a Kuranta for stamina.\n:\nMost Kuranta originate from Kazimierz; a land torn between traditionalist feudal beliefs and modern capitalism. As such, many Kuranta subscribe to one of these ideals, of the old honour, or the new progress. Of course, some choose a different path; a middle path, or neither path. \n\n\n\n\n\\column\n\n#### Kuranta Traits\n\n***Creature Type:*** You are a Humanoid.\n\n***Size:*** Kuranta are marginally taller than some other races, clocking in between 5 and a half and 6 feet on average, but pack a lot of dense muscle into their frames; thus, they weigh about 190 pounds on average. Their size is Medium. \n\n***Life Expectancy:*** Kuranta reach adulthood around the age of 18, and have a life expectancy of around 80 years. \n\n***Speed:*** Your base walking speed is 30 feet.\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Constitution Score increases by 2, and two other scores of your choice increase by 1.\n\n#### Kuranta Features\nAs a Kuranta, you gain the following Features:\n\n##### Ever Onward\nNo matter their destiny, no matter their objective, no matter how hopeless; the Kuranta charge onwards. \n:\nWhen you would be subjected to an effect that would decrease your Speed or prevent you from moving, you may expend 1d8 Hit Points as a Reaction to ignore that aspect of the effect. All other aspects of the triggering effect (such as Damage dealt, and other Conditions) are applied as normal.\n:\n\n\n##### Run Them Down\nKuranta are naturally suited to battle by their stunning speed, opening up the opportunities for those lightning fast clashes that make the Kuranta Knights of Kazimierz so enthralling to watch. \n:\nYou may take the Dash Action as a Bonus Action; when you do so using this Feature, you lose 1d8 Hit Points.\n\n{{imageMaskEdge1,--offset:2%,--rotation:90\n  <img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/e/ea/Platinum_Elite_2.png' \n  style='position:absolute;top:200px;right:100px;width:1100px;clip-path:rect(12% auto 70% auto);' />\n}}\n\n{{imageMaskEdge1,--offset:12%,--rotation:0\n  <img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/e/ea/Platinum_Elite_2.png' \n  style='position:absolute;top:200px;right:100px;width:1100px;clip-path:rect(48% auto auto auto);' />\n}}\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}\n\n\\page\n\n{{wide\n##### Until the Last Breath\nKuranta are skilled fighters; this is something everybody knows. When you see their blinding speed and bravery, it is easy to assume those are the only reasons. Under the skin, however, the hidden engine of their power pulses hot; they don’t have to beat you, just outlast you. \n:\nYou may activate this Feature as a Bonus Action; for the next minute you gain 1d6 + your Constitution Modifier (minimum of 1) Temporary Hit Points at the beginning of each of your Turns. Once you have used this Feature, you may not do so again until you have completed a Long Rest. \n\n##### Ancient Versatility\nThe Ancient Species seized the world of Terra from the Teekaz, and have since spread all over its surface, to all its climes and domains. As such, those of an Ancient Species possess a versatility not seen in the Teekaz. Choose one from the following benefits when you select this Species:\n\n**Durable.** Your Hit Point maximum increases by an amount equal to your Level. Whenever you gain a Level thereafter, your Hit Point maximum increases by an additional Hit Point.\n\n**Reliable.** You gain Proficiency in one Skill of your choice.\n\n**Tenacious.** You can add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to any Saving Throw you are not Proficient in.\n}}\n\n<img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/c/cb/Wild_Mane_Elite_2.png' \n  style='position:absolute;top:270px;right:30px;width:800px' />\n  \n  {{pageNumber,auto}}\n\n\\page"
