    "content": "<h3>Banshee</h3>\n<p>Even amongst the Sarkaz, the Banshee are unusual. To begin, a majority of Banshee are female; male Banshee are principally rare, with their current Great Banshee being one such specimen. Despite the fact that their current de jure leader is male, Banshee society is matriarchal, due in no small part to the fact there simply aren't many men. Unlike their sister Species in the Sarkaz, Banshee do not have tails, but do have horns which grow into branch-like shapes, complete with offshoots. They also possess wing-like feathered structures on their head, which can sometimes lead to them being mistaken for Liberi, and are widely considered to be highly physically attractive. There is, however, no mistaking the power of a Banshee. Their supreme oral Arts are renowned and feared, and many Banshee can cast or manifest Arts by simply speaking or singing.<br>In Sarkaz society, Banshees are considered to be guardians, or shepherds, of the dead, guiding the consciousness of the Sarkaz back to their afterlife within the Nephesh. To hear the Banshee's elegy is to know your life is at an end, and they will take you on winds of song to your afterlife. For particularly prominent figures or moments, Banshee have a bone whistle that is blown to signify the passing of such a moment, and the lamentation it represents. Due to their associations with death, the sound of that bonewhistle is feared across Terra.</p>\n<h4>Banshee Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Charisma Score increases by 1.</p>\n<h4>Banshee Features</h4>\n<p>As a Banshee, you gain the following Features:</p>\n<h5>Shepherd of the Dead</h5>\n<p>While your song can carry away the souls of the Sarkaz to the afterlife, it can also serve as an anchor point, fixing the life of a being to the earth. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p><strong>Death Ward.</strong> You can cast the Death Ward Art using a Bone Whistle or your singing as the Casting Unit, but only as a Ritual.</p>\n<p><strong>Tool Proficiency.</strong> You are Proficient in Instrument (Bone Whistle) and Instrument (Microphone), and gain both as starting Equipment. The Bone Whistle costs the same as a flute to replace, but can only be acquired from Banshee craftswomen.</p>\n<h5>Voice of Ruin</h5>\n<p>The Banshee of the Sarkaz are lethal and beautiful in equal measure. Their voice can sooth hearts or stop them, their song calm seas or crack walls.<br>You learn the Arts from the Banshee Arts Pool; these are Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability for these Arts; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Banshee\n\nEven amongst the Sarkaz, the Banshee are unusual. To begin, a majority of Banshee are female; male Banshee are principally rare, with their current Great Banshee being one such specimen. Despite the fact that their current de jure leader is male, Banshee society is matriarchal, due in no small part to the fact there simply aren't many men. Unlike their sister Species in the Sarkaz, Banshee do not have tails, but do have horns which grow into branch-like shapes, complete with offshoots. They also possess wing-like feathered structures on their head, which can sometimes lead to them being mistaken for Liberi, and are widely considered to be highly physically attractive. There is, however, no mistaking the power of a Banshee. Their supreme oral Arts are renowned and feared, and many Banshee can cast or manifest Arts by simply speaking or singing.\n:\nIn Sarkaz society, Banshees are considered to be guardians, or shepherds, of the dead, guiding the consciousness of the Sarkaz back to their afterlife within the Nephesh. To hear the Banshee's elegy is to know your life is at an end, and they will take you on winds of song to your afterlife. For particularly prominent figures or moments, Banshee have a bone whistle that is blown to signify the passing of such a moment, and the lamentation it represents. Due to their associations with death, the sound of that bonewhistle is feared across Terra.\n\n#### Banshee Traits\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Charisma Score increases by 1.\n\n#### Banshee Features\nAs a Banshee, you gain the following Features:\n\n##### Shepherd of the Dead\nWhile your song can carry away the souls of the Sarkaz to the afterlife, it can also serve as an anchor point, fixing the life of a being to the earth. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Death Ward.** You can cast the Death Ward Art using a Bone Whistle or your singing as the Casting Unit, but only as a Ritual.\n\n**Tool Proficiency.** You are Proficient in Instrument (Bone Whistle) and Instrument (Microphone), and gain both as starting Equipment. The Bone Whistle costs the same as a flute to replace, but can only be acquired from Banshee craftswomen.\n\n\\column\n\n##### Voice of Ruin \nThe Banshee of the Sarkaz are lethal and beautiful in equal measure. Their voice can sooth hearts or stop them, their song calm seas or crack walls.\n:\nYou learn the Arts from the Banshee Arts Pool; these are Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability for these Arts; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts.\n\n<img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/d/d5/Nasti_Lunorey.png' \n  style='position:absolute;top:240px;right:-150px;width:750px' />\n  \n  {{pageNumber,auto}}\n  \n\n\\page\n\n{{wide"
