    "content": "<h3>Djall</h3>\n<p>The Djaj (singular: Djall) were once one of the more feared tribes of the Sarkaz Royal Courts, both for their proficiency with psychic Arts and for their ability to feed on the thoughts of others. The stronger the emotion, the more sustanance a Djall can derive from it, leading them to resort to physical and psychological torture to generate those strong emotions. The exact means by which they \"consume\" thought is not well documented; in the past, their reputation was too fearsome to attempt study. In the modern age, Djaj are considerably rarer than other members of the Royal Court, as their constant exposure to the negative emotion in and around Kazdel has caused the vast majority to emigrate to isolated lands, away from where they might feasibly be studied.<br>Physically, Djaj are shorter in stature, with long whip-like tails, large pointed ears, and large upwards horns that curve inwards. Their less physical nature than other Sarkaz causes many to underestimate them; a final, agonizing mistake their minds never recover from.</p>\n<h4>Djall Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Charisma Score increases by 1.</p>\n<h4>Djall Features</h4>\n<p>As a Djall, you gain the following Features:</p>\n<h5>Cognitovore</h5>\n<p>As you walk the streets of any location, you cannot help but brush your mind against others; a mere taste of what lies inside their skulls. With just a little urging, you can dig deeper, like a bird pecking for worms, and coax free the sustenance your crave. You can do so gently, excising pain and misery; or you can rip it free, leaving a raw psychological wound for you to exploit.<br>You can sense the surface thoughts of any Creature within 15 feet, as long as that Creature has an Intelligence Score greater than 3, and is not an Undead, Plant, or Construct. You learn how these Creatures are feeling in simple terms, such as Angry or Sad.<br>As an Action, you can attempt to probe deeper into the thoughts of a Creature you can read the surface thoughts of. That Creature must make an Intelligence Saving Throw (DC = 8 + Your Charisma Bonus + Proficiency Bonus OR Your Spell Save DC) to resist the effect; a Creature can choose to fail this Saving Throw.</p>\n<p>On a successful Save, you learn nothing, and the Creature becomes immune to this effect for 24 hours. On a failed Saving Throw, you gain insight into what they are currently thinking about, its reasoning for its actions, and something that it thinks about often (such as a loved one, or a major point of stress) for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>A target Creature knows you are probing its mind, and can reattempt the Saving Throw at the end of each of their Turns, ending the effect on a success. You can only probe the thoughts of one Creature at a time in this way; using this effect on another Creature ends the effect on the first.<br>Additionally, when a Creature fails the initial Saving Throw against this effect, you can consume a thought gently or roughly. If you consume a thought gently, that Creature is considered to be under the effect of the Heroism Art until you stop probing deeper into their thoughts. If you consume a thought roughly, that Creature is Dazed until you stop probing deeper into their thoughts.</p>\n<h5>Key to the Heart</h5>\n<p>The Djall's original fearsome reputation comes from their innate proficiency for Psychic Arts. When facing a Djaj, your own mind is not your ally.<br>You learn all levelled Arts from the Psychic Arts Pool; these are considered to be Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts.<br>If you gain the ability to cast any of these Psychic Arts in another way, you instead gain a permanent +1 to your Spell Save DC and Spell Attack Rolls when casting that Art.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Djall\n\nThe Djaj (singular: Djall) were once one of the more feared tribes of the Sarkaz Royal Courts, both for their proficiency with psychic Arts and for their ability to feed on the thoughts of others. The stronger the emotion, the more sustanance a Djall can derive from it, leading them to resort to physical and psychological torture to generate those strong emotions. The exact means by which they \"consume\" thought is not well documented; in the past, their reputation was too fearsome to attempt study. In the modern age, Djaj are considerably rarer than other members of the Royal Court, as their constant exposure to the negative emotion in and around Kazdel has caused the vast majority to emigrate to isolated lands, away from where they might feasibly be studied.\n:\nPhysically, Djaj are shorter in stature, with long whip-like tails, large pointed ears, and large upwards horns that curve inwards. Their less physical nature than other Sarkaz causes many to underestimate them; a final, agonizing mistake their minds never recover from. \n\n#### Djall Traits\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Charisma Score increases by 1.\n\n#### Djall Features\nAs a Djall, you gain the following Features:\n\n{{imageMaskEdge4,--offset:3%,--rotation:90\n   <img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/thumb/Nymph.png/1024px-Nymph.png?de28b4' \n  style='position:absolute;top:525px;right:315px;width:500px' />\n}}\n\n\n\n\n\\column\n\n##### Cognitovore\nAs you walk the streets of any location, you cannot help but brush your mind against others; a mere taste of what lies inside their skulls. With just a little urging, you can dig deeper, like a bird pecking for worms, and coax free the sustenance your crave. You can do so gently, excising pain and misery; or you can rip it free, leaving a raw psychological wound for you to exploit.\n:\nYou can sense the surface thoughts of any Creature within 15 feet, as long as that Creature has an Intelligence Score greater than 3, and is not an Undead, Plant, or Construct. You learn how these Creatures are feeling in simple terms, such as Angry or Sad. \n:\nAs an Action, you can attempt to probe deeper into the thoughts of a Creature you can read the surface thoughts of. That Creature must make an Intelligence Saving Throw (DC = 8 + Your Charisma Bonus + Proficiency Bonus OR Your Spell Save DC) to resist the effect; a Creature can choose to fail this Saving Throw. \n\nOn a successful Save, you learn nothing, and the Creature becomes immune to this effect for 24 hours. On a failed Saving Throw, you gain insight into what they are currently thinking about, its reasoning for its actions, and something that it thinks about often (such as a loved one, or a major point of stress) for 1 minute. \n\nA target Creature knows you are probing its mind, and can reattempt the Saving Throw at the end of each of their Turns, ending the effect on a success. You can only probe the thoughts of one Creature at a time in this way; using this effect on another Creature ends the effect on the first. \n:\nAdditionally, when a Creature fails the initial Saving Throw against this effect, you can consume a thought gently or roughly. If you consume a thought gently, that Creature is considered to be under the effect of the Heroism Art until you stop probing deeper into their thoughts. If you consume a thought roughly, that Creature is Dazed until you stop probing deeper into their thoughts.\n\n\n\n##### Key to the Heart\nThe Djall's original fearsome reputation comes from their innate proficiency for Psychic Arts. When facing a Djaj, your own mind is not your ally.\n:\nYou learn all levelled Arts from the Psychic Arts Pool; these are considered to be Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts.\n:\nIf you gain the ability to cast any of these Psychic Arts in another way, you instead gain a permanent +1 to your Spell Save DC and Spell Attack Rolls when casting that Art.\n\n\n\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}\n\n\\page\n\n{{wide"
