    "content": "<h3>Nachzehrer</h3>\n<p>On a cursory examination, one could confuse a Nachzehrer for a Vampire; tall and slender in stature, and pale in skin. Unlike Vampires, however, Nachzehrer do possess the horns typically associated with Sarkaz.<br>The most notable trait of the Nachzehrer is the very one that has given rise to their association with war and death; their ability to \"eat\" the fallen by absorbing all the nutrients and mass left in the corpse, leaving it a dessicated husk.  When they do so, they learn the recent memories of those they consume.</p>\n<p>For many Nachzehrer, this is a deeply spiritual and religious act; their death is not the end so long as they are consumed by another. Every Nachzehrer is nourished by they who came before. Some Nachzehrer take this a step further, physically consuming the flesh of their fallen enemies and comrades.</p>\n<h4>Nachzehrer Traits</h4>\n<p><strong><em>Ability Score Improvement:</em></strong> Your Constitution Score increases by 1.</p>\n<h4>Nachzehrer Features</h4>\n<p>As a Nachzehrer, you gain the following Features:</p>\n<h5>In Death, Life; In Life, Death</h5>\n<p>The Nachzehrer are called the personification of war by some. For many, that invokes the image of powerful warriors laying waste to their foes. The Nachzehrer fit this bill, but it is not for this reason that they embody war; the Nachzehrer feast upon death to continue, just as war does.<br>Once per Short Rest, you may \"consume\" a corpse by absorbing all of the nutrients from it over the course of a minute, leaving it a deflated husk; you must remain in contact with the corpse for the entire duration. When you do so, you gain Rot equal to the CR or Level of that Creature (minimum 1). The maximum Rot you can have is equal to your Character Level. In addition, when you do this, you can ask that corpse a single question, as if it was under the effect of the Speak with Dead Art; it must be as truthful as it is possible for it to be in its answer.<br>When you cast a Necrotic Art, you may expend any amount of your Rot (no Action required); you gain a Bonus to your Spell Save DC and Spell Attack Rolls for the casting of the Art equal to the amount of Rot expended.</p>\n<h5>Rot and Ruin</h5>\n<p>Relentless, gruesome, ruinous; all words that could be used to describe the Nachzehrer and their withering Arts.<br>You learn the Arts from the Necrotic Arts Pool; these are Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts.</p>",
    "rawSource": "### Nachzehrer\nOn a cursory examination, one could confuse a Nachzehrer for a Vampire; tall and slender in stature, and pale in skin. Unlike Vampires, however, Nachzehrer do possess the horns typically associated with Sarkaz. \n:\nThe most notable trait of the Nachzehrer is the very one that has given rise to their association with war and death; their ability to \"eat\" the fallen by absorbing all the nutrients and mass left in the corpse, leaving it a dessicated husk.  When they do so, they learn the recent memories of those they consume. \n\nFor many Nachzehrer, this is a deeply spiritual and religious act; their death is not the end so long as they are consumed by another. Every Nachzehrer is nourished by they who came before. Some Nachzehrer take this a step further, physically consuming the flesh of their fallen enemies and comrades.\n\n#### Nachzehrer Traits\n\n***Ability Score Improvement:*** Your Constitution Score increases by 1.\n\n#### Nachzehrer Features\nAs a Nachzehrer, you gain the following Features:\n\n##### In Death, Life; In Life, Death\nThe Nachzehrer are called the personification of war by some. For many, that invokes the image of powerful warriors laying waste to their foes. The Nachzehrer fit this bill, but it is not for this reason that they embody war; the Nachzehrer feast upon death to continue, just as war does.\n:\nOnce per Short Rest, you may \"consume\" a corpse by absorbing all of the nutrients from it over the course of a minute, leaving it a deflated husk; you must remain in contact with the corpse for the entire duration. When you do so, you gain Rot equal to the CR or Level of that Creature (minimum 1). The maximum Rot you can have is equal to your Character Level. In addition, when you do this, you can ask that corpse a single question, as if it was under the effect of the Speak with Dead Art; it must be as truthful as it is possible for it to be in its answer.\n:\nWhen you cast a Necrotic Art, you may expend any amount of your Rot (no Action required); you gain a Bonus to your Spell Save DC and Spell Attack Rolls for the casting of the Art equal to the amount of Rot expended. \n\n\\column\n\n##### Rot and Ruin\nRelentless, gruesome, ruinous; all words that could be used to describe the Nachzehrer and their withering Arts.\n:\nYou learn the Arts from the Necrotic Arts Pool; these are Sarkaz Arts. If you do not have the Ability to cast Arts in another way, Charisma is your Arts Casting Ability; you do not need a weapon with the Casting Unit Property to cast these Arts. \n\n\n<img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/Nadine.png?c2f738' \n  style='position:absolute;top:220px;right:-180px;width:800px;clip-path:rect(auto auto auto auto);' />\n\n\n\n\n\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}\n\n  \n\\page"
